  "borough": "Tower Hamlets",
  "description": "General maintenance to the roof and exterior, in order to bring the building in line with current building regulations for tall buildings. This maintenance consists of:Replacement of timber cladding and glazing on new penthouse extensions with zinc and new windows, replacement of penthouse roof terrace timber decking with concrete tiles.Replacement of existing timber planks around clothes-drying areas with visually identical non-flammable panels.Access balcony steel balustrades to be repainted, or replaced like-for-like if excessively corroded.Replacement of timber decking from roof of main entrance canopy with concrete tiles.Exchange rotten timber planks over ground floor entrance bridge with composite timber ones, and substitute glass balustrade with stainless steel handrail.",
